-- PhiSQL equivalent of general-purpose.json, side by side for comparison.
--
-- PhiSQL v0.1 covers the redaction subset and compiles to the same Phileas
-- JSON schema. A few details of the JSON policy are not yet expressible in
-- v0.1 and are noted below:
--   * v0.1 has no PERSON entity, so personsName is expressed as the
--     FIRST_NAME + SURNAME pair (the v0.1 substitution for PERSON).
--   * Detector-confidence thresholds use a 0..1 scale in PhiSQL.
--   * The creditCard "onlyValidCreditCards" flag has no v0.1 keyword.
-- Plain REDACT uses Phileas's default redaction format ({{{REDACTED-%t}}}),
-- which is the format the JSON policy sets explicitly.

POLICY general_purpose;

REDACT FIRST_NAME, SURNAME WITH REDACT WHERE CONFIDENCE > 0.70;

REDACT PHONE_NUMBER, EMAIL_ADDRESS, SSN, IP_ADDRESS, URL,
       IBAN_CODE, PASSPORT_NUMBER, DRIVERS_LICENSE, CREDIT_CARD
  WITH REDACT;
